meta {
  name: Stream Deployment Events (SSE)
  type: http
  seq: 5
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/deployments/{{deploymentId}}/events
  body: none
  auth: none
}

headers {
  X-Dev-User-ID: {{devUserId}}
  Accept: text/event-stream
}

docs {
  Server-Sent Events stream. The connection stays open until one of:
    - the deployment reaches a terminal phase (ready / failed),
    - the orchestrator reports the Application is gone,
    - the client disconnects,
    - the 10-minute hard cap is reached.

  Event types emitted:
    event: state    — { deployment_id, phase, revision, healthy, message, source }
    event: warn     — { message }   (transient upstream errors; stream stays open)
    event: end      — { reason, phase? }

  V1 implementation polls Orchestrator.Status every 2 seconds. Sprint 2
  swaps polling for push events from Argo CD webhooks.

  IMPORTANT: Bruno's response viewer does not natively render SSE.
  Use curl for a proper interactive view:

    curl -N -H "X-Dev-User-ID: <uuid>" \
         http://localhost:8080/api/v1/deployments/<id>/events
}
